            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Nero's Early Life</strong><br>\nNero was born on December 15, 37 AD, in the city of Antium, now known as Anzio, Italy. His full name at birth was Lucius Domitius Ahenobarbus. Nero's mother, Agrippina the Younger, was the sister of Emperor Caligula, and his father was Gnaeus Domitius Ahenobarbus, a member of the Roman elite. After his father's death, Nero's mother married her uncle, Emperor Claudius, making Nero heir to the Roman throne. Nero was well-educated, studying under the philosopher Seneca, and he became emperor at the tender age of 17.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Rise to Power</strong><br>\nNero became the emperor of Rome in 54 AD after the death of his stepfather, Claudius, who was thought to have been poisoned by Agrippina. Initially, Nero ruled with the guidance of his mother, his tutor Seneca, and the Praetorian Prefect Burrus. During the early years of his reign, Nero was known for his generous political gestures, such as eliminating unfair taxes and allowing slaves to file complaints against their masters. He was also popular for his public performances and chariot races.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Governing Rome</strong><br>\nAs emperor, Nero made significant administrative decisions. He focused on diplomacy, trade, and enhancing the cultural life of the empire. He increased Rome's interactions with Greece and tried to implement Greek culture into Roman life. His rule brought various public works, including the construction of theaters and promoting athletic games. However, his administrative periods were also marked by extravagance and hedonism, which later became the focus of criticism.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
